methods.doc:
Returns the delivery post office for a post code, from Pakistan Post's
directory of about 2,560 offices.

Unlike {@link Postal.GetCity}, which only answers for codes in the cities
pakdatakit lists, this knows every delivery office, including those in
towns and villages.

```csharp
Postal.GetPostOffice("48330");
// PostOffice { Code = 48330, Office = Dulmial, Town = Dulmial, District = , Province = Punjab }
```

fields.doc:
Points for each part of an address, in order. They add up to 100. A
postal code scores in full only when it is a known post office code;
an unknown one scores 5.

methods.doc:
Adds sales tax to an amount, or splits it out when
{@link SalesTaxOptions.Inclusive} is set.

Give a {@link SalesTaxOptions.Rate}, or a
{@link SalesTaxOptions.Province} (and {@link SalesTaxOptions.Kind},
default services, and a date) to use the standard rate from
{@link SalesTax.GetRate}. The tax is rounded half up to the paisa.

```csharp
SalesTax.Calculate(1000, new SalesTaxOptions { Rate = 18 }); // Net = 1000, Tax = 180, Gross = 1180, Rate = 18
SalesTax.Calculate(1000, new SalesTaxOptions { Province = "Punjab", Date = "2026-11-18" });
// Net = 1000, Tax = 160, Gross = 1160, Rate = 16,
// Source = { Id = "sales-tax-rates", EffectiveFrom = "2019-07-01", … }
```

